  Quote of the Week:

  Saint Ignatius Loyola, Spanish soldier and founder of the Jesuit Order, 
1522:
  "To arrive at the truth in all things, we ought always to be ready to 
believe that what seems to us white, is black if the hierarchical Church so 
defines it."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Stormy winter gave way to fragrant spring, and Tumijin Khaan made ready to 
carry out his urgent assignments.  He prepared his armies to defend Baikal 
and the surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Tumijin Khaan for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Urians (#228) has just recently wandered into Tien Shan from Hindu Kush.


  Here is the financial report for Tumijin Khaan's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Tumijin Khaan was 
left with 11 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Barant
To: Tumijin Khaan

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I prepared my armies to defend Tien Shan and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Barant


